        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ചുണ്ട്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ചുണ്ട് (cuṇṭŭ) — \"a lip\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Inherited, matching Tamil cuṇṭu. It is the lip of a mouth and also the beak of a bird — one shape for the pointed front edge of the face, whatever the face belongs to."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The same word reaches the spout of a jug, so a Malayalam pot has lips much as an English one does. That figure was arrived at twice over, on two sides of the world, from the same obvious resemblance."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ണ്ട cluster in the middle is the retroflex ṇ running straight into a ṭ, made with the tongue curled back, and it is worth slowing down for."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three, and this one belongs to birds as well."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
