        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: എല്ല്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "എല്ല് (ellŭ) — \"a bone\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Inherited, and Tamil says elumpu for the same thing — close enough to hear the shared ancestor, far enough apart to show the two languages went on working after they separated."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Malayalam shortened where Tamil kept the extra piece, which is the direction these two usually run. Set the two side by side often enough and the pattern starts to predict itself."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The doubled ll is held, and the ŭ closes it, so the whole word is over in about the time it takes to say the English one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and the frame is done: the neck, the back, a lip, a nail, a bone."
            }
          ]
        },
